crisp-mcp es un servidor de investigación cualitativa asistida por IA que utiliza aprendizaje automático y análisis de vibraciones","fr":"crisp-mcp est un serveur de recherche qualitative assistée par IA qui utilise le machine learning et l''analyse de vibrations","de":"crisp-mcp ist ein Server für qualitative Forschung, der von künstlicher Intelligenz unterstützt wird und Machine Learning sowie Vibrationen-Analytics verwendet","pt":"O que é CRISP-MCP? É uma ferramenta de análise qualitativa que utiliza IA para ligar narrativas textuais e dados numéricos","ru":"Что такое CRISP-MCP? Это инструмент качественного анализа, который использует ИИ Агенты для соединения текстовых нарративов и числовых данных","ar":"ما هو CRISP-MCP؟ هو أداة تحليل نوعية تستخدم الإيجابية الاصطناعية لربط السرد النصي والبيانات الرقمية"},"features":{"en":["Utilizes the CRISP-T MCP server for qualitative analysis","Supports computational triangulation for data validation","Employs grounded theory-inspired coding for text analysis","Provides tools for corpus management and text coding","Exposes several tools for numeric analysis","Falls back to crisp-cli skill if CRISP-T MCP server is unavailable"],"zh":["计算三角测量","基于扎根理论的编码","文本编码工具","数值分析工具","CRISP-T MCP 服务器集成"],"ja":["計算三角測量","根拠に基づくコード化","テキストコーディングツール","数値分析ツール","CRISP-T MCP サーバー統合"],"ko":["계산 삼각 측정","근거에 기반한 코딩","텍스트 코딩 도구","수치 분석 도구","CRISP-T MCP 서버 통합"],"es":["Servidor de investigación cualitativa con aprendizaje automático","Análisis de vibraciones para triangular datos computacionales","Teoría fundamentada para codificar textos y datos numéricos","Herramientas para gestión de corpus y codificación de textos","Soporte para análisis numérico y codificación inspirada en teoría fundamentada"],"fr":["Serveur de recherche qualitative avec machine learning","Analyse de vibrations pour la triangulation de données computationnelles","Théorie ancrée pour coder les textes et les données numériques","Outils pour la gestion de corpus et la codification de textes","Prise en charge de l''analyse numérique et de la codification inspirée par la théorie ancrée"],"de":["Server für qualitative Forschung mit Machine Learning","Vibrationen-Analytics für die Verbindung von computergestützten Daten","Grounded Theory für die Kodierung von Texten und numerischen Daten","Werkzeuge für die Verwaltung von Corpora und die Kodierung von Texten","Unterstützung für numerische Analyse und kodierungsinspirierte Theorie"],"pt":["Análise qualitativa com vibração analítica","Triangulação computacional para ligar narrativas textuais e dados numéricos","Ferramentas de gerenciamento de corpus","Codificação de texto inspirada na teoria fundamentada","Análise numérica com exposição de ferramentas","Integração com o servidor CRISP-T MCP"],"ru":["Качественный анализ с вибрационной аналитикой","Компьютерная триангуляция для соединения текстовых нарративов и числовых данных","Инструменты управления корпусом","Кодирование текста, вдохновленное основанной теорией","Числовой анализ с экспозицией инструментов","Интеграция с сервером CRISP-T MCP"],"ar":["تحليل نوعي مع تحليل التأرجح","ثلاثية الحوسبة لربط السرد النصي والبيانات الرقمية","أدوات إدارة المجموعة","ترميز النص الملهم بنظرية القاعدة","تحليل رقمي مع عرض أدوات","التكامل مع خادم CRISP-T MCP"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use crisp-mcp","crisp-mcp setup guide","crisp-mcp alternative","crisp-mcp vs machine learning","what is crisp-mcp","crisp-mcp install","crisp-mcp qualitative research","crisp-mcp NLP analysis","crisp-mcp Hacktoberfest"],"zh":["CRISP-T MCP 服务器","AI 辅助质性研究","计算三角测量","基于扎根理论的编码","文本编码","数值分析","质性研究工具","AI 研究工具"],"ja":["CRISP-T MCP サーバー","AI エージェントによる質的研究","計算三角測量","根拠に基づくコード化","テキストコーディング","数値分析","質的研究ツール","AI 研究ツール"],"ko":["CRISP-T MCP 서버","AI 에이전트 기반의 질적 연구","계산 삼각 측정","근거에 기반한 코딩","텍스트 코딩","수치 분석","질적 연구 도구","AI 연구 도구"],"es":["crisp-mcp","investigación cualitativa","aprendizaje automático","análisis de vibraciones","teoría fundamentada","gestión de corpus","codificación de textos","análisis numérico","herramientas de investigación","IA para investigación"],"fr":["crisp-mcp","recherche qualitative","machine learning","analyse de vibrations","théorie ancrée","gestion de corpus","codification de textes","analyse numérique","outils de recherche","IA pour la recherche"],"de":["crisp-mcp","qualitative Forschung","Machine Learning","Vibrationen-Analytics","Grounded Theory","Corpus-Verwaltung","Textkodierung","numerische Analyse","Forschungstools","KI für Forschung"],"pt":["CRISP-MCP","análise qualitativa","vibração analítica","triangulação computacional","ferramentas de IA","gerenciamento de corpus","codificação de texto","análise numérica","servidor CRISP-T MCP","Hacktoberfest"],"ru":["CRISP-MCP","качественный анализ","вибрационная аналитика","компьютерная триангуляция","инструменты ИИ Агенты","управление корпусом","кодирование текста","числовой анализ","сервер CRISP-T MCP","Hacktoberfest"],"ar":["CRISP-MCP","تحليل نوعي","تحليل التأرجح","ثلاثية الحوسبة","أدوات الإيجابية الاصطناعية","إدارة المجموعة","ترميز النص","تحليل رقمي","خادم CRISP-T MCP","Hacktoberfest"]}},"owner":"dermatologist","repo":"crisp-t","repoPath":"dermatologist/crisp-t","stars":8,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-26T22:06:45Z","topics":["hacktoberfest","machine-learning","nlp","qualitative-research"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"crisp-mcp","description":"Use the CRISP‑T MCP server to run a full qualitative analysis workflow linking textual narratives and numeric data.","bodyPreview":"## Summary\n\n**Goal:**\nUse the CRISP‑T MCP server to run a full, *documented* qualitative analysis workflow—linking textual narratives and numeric data—using computational triangulation and grounded theory–inspired coding.\n\nThis skill assumes:\n\n- The **CRISP‑T MCP server** is available as an MCP server called crisp.\n- **If you do not find the crisp MCP server, inform the user and use crisp-cli skill instead.**\n- The server exposes several tools for **corpus management, text coding, numeric analys","body":"## Summary\n\n**Goal:**\nUse the CRISP‑T MCP server to run a full, *documented* qualitative analysis workflow—linking textual narratives and numeric data—using computational triangulation and grounded theory–inspired coding.\n\nThis skill assumes:\n\n- The **CRISP‑T MCP server** is available as an MCP server called crisp.\n- **If you do not find the crisp MCP server, inform the user and use crisp-cli skill instead.**\n- The server exposes several tools for **corpus management, text coding, numeric analysis, triangulation, and export**\n- The model can **discover tools at runtime** and adapt to the actual tool list\n\nUse this skill when the user wants to:\n\n- Explore and code qualitative data (e.g., interviews, narratives, open‑ended survey responses)\n- Triangulate qualitative codes with quantitative variables\n- Produce **transparent, reproducible outputs** (memos, codebooks, matrices, summaries)\n\n---\n\n## Intended users and scenarios\n\n- **Qualitative / mixed‑methods researchers** working with text + numeric data\n\nTypical scenarios:\n\n- Coding COVID‑era patient narratives and linking them to open‑source epidemiological data\n- Triangulating interview themes with survey scores or EHR‑derived indicators\n- Building theory from mixed text–numeric corpora using CRISP‑T stages\n\n---\n\n## MCP server and tools\n\n### Server\n\n- **Server name (example):** `crisp-t`\n- **Protocol:** Model Context Protocol (MCP) via stdio (e.g., `crisp-mcp`)\n\n> **Important:**\n> Use ./workspace as the working directory for all artifacts, if not explicitly specified. Create it if it does not exist.\n> Always **discover** the available tools from the CRISP‑T MCP server first, then map them to the workflow below.\n> Tool names in this file are **illustrative**; prefer the *actual* tool names and schemas exposed by the server.\n\n## Recommended steps\n* Import data into CRISP-T corpus and dataframe.\n* Perform linking between text and numeric data using various methods (id based, keyword based, time based, embedding based).\n* Explore text data using various methods (e.g., topic modeling, keyword extraction, sentiment analysis, visualizations).\n* Explore numeric data using various methods (e.g., summary statistics, classification, clustering, regression, association, visualizations, TDA, etc.).\n* Perform cross modal analysis using linked text and numeric data (e.g., text features as predictors for numeric outcomes, numeric features as predictors for text outcomes, etc.).\n* Add manual connections between text documents and numeric rows if needed to support theory driven analysis.\n* Derive insights from the analysis and document them.\n\n### Expected tool capabilities (illustrative)\n\nWhen you discover tools from the `crisp-t` MCP server, look for tools that correspond to the following capabilities:\n\n1. **Project and configuration**\n   - **List / load projects** (e.g., `list_projects`, `load_project`)\n   - **List / configure data sources** (text + numeric)\n\n2. **Textual data operations**\n   - **List text sources** (e.g., documents, transcripts, narrative files)\n   - **Fetch text segments** (e.g., by document, case, or segment ID)\n   - **Apply or update codes** to segments\n   - **List codes / categories / codebook**\n\n3. **Numeric / structured data operations**\n   - **List numeric datasets** (e.g., CSVs, tables)\n   - **Fetch rows / variables** for a given case or group\n   - **Run basic summaries or models** (e.g., descriptive stats, correlations)\n\n4. **Triangulation / integration**\n   - **Link coded text segments to numeric data** by case ID or key\n   - **Generate triangulation matrices** (codes × variables, cases × themes, etc.)\n   - **Compute simple indicators** (e.g., frequency, co‑occurrence, association)\n\n5. **Memoing and export**\n   - **Create / update analytic memos**\n   - **Export codebooks, matrices, and summaries** (e.g., CSV, JSON, Markdown)\n   - **Save session context or analysis snapshots**\n\nWhen using this skill, you should:\n\n- **Inspect tool descriptions and schemas**\n- **Prefer higher‑level CRISP‑T tools** (e.g., “triangulate”, “inspect”, “sense‑make”) over low‑level primitives when available\n- **Avoid guessing tool parameters**—use the schema and ask the user when needed\n\n---\n\n## Inputs\n\nThe user may provide some or all of the following. If missing, ask concise clarification questions.\n\n- **Research question / focus**\n  - `research_question`: short description of what they want to understand or explain\n- **Project / dataset selection**\n  - `project_name` or `project_id`\n  - `text_source_pattern` (e.g., “patient_narratives”, “interviews_*”)\n  - `numeric_dataset_name` (e.g., “covid_metrics.csv”, “survey_scores”)\n- **Methodological preferences**\n  - `coding_style`: open coding, focused coding, or using an existing codebook\n  - `triangulation_focus`: e.g., “compare themes by age group”, “link narratives to hospitalization status”\n- **Output preferences**\n  - `output_format`: Markdown, CSV, JSON, or mixed\n  - `audience`: “methods‑savvy colleague”, “student”, “grant reviewer”, etc.\n\nIf the user is vague, default to:\n\n- Open coding → focused coding\n- Simple triangulation (themes × one or two key numeric variables)\n- Markdown summaries plus CSV exports where supported\n\n---\n\n## Outputs\n\nThis skill should aim to produce:\n\n1. **Analytic memo**\n   - Research question and context\n   - Data sources used (text + numeric)\n   - Coding approach and key categories\n   - Triangulation findings (convergences, divergences, surprises)\n   - Limitations and next steps\n\n2. **Structured artifacts** (when tools support them)\n   - Codebook (codes, definitions, examples)\n   - Triangulation matrix (e.g., codes × variables)\n   - Exported files (CSV/JSON/Markdown) referenced in the memo\n\n3. **Reproducible trace**\n   - Clear description of which MCP tools were called\n   - Parameters used (e.g., filters, variables, thresholds)\n   - Any important analytic decisions made during the session\n\n---\n\n## High‑level workflow\n\nYou should follow this workflow, adapting to the actual CRISP‑T tools you discover.\n\n### 1. Clarify research focus and context\n\n1. **Summarize the user’s goal** in 2–3 sentences.\n2. If unclear, ask **one or two** focused questions:\n   - **Example:** “Which is more important right now: exploring themes, or linking themes to numeric outcomes?”\n3. Record the clarified research question in the analytic memo.\n\n### 2. Discover CRISP‑T MCP tools and project context\n\n1. **List available tools** from the `crisp-t` MCP server.\n2. Identify tools that correspond to:\n   - Project management\n   - Text operations\n   - Numeric operations\n   - Triangulation\n   - Memoing / export\n3. If available, **list projects** and either:\n   - Load the project specified by the user, or\n   - Present a short list and ask the user to choose.\n\nDocument in the memo:\n\n- Which project was loaded\n- Which tools will be used and for what purpose\n\n### 3. Inspect data sources (text + numeric)\n\n1. Use project / data tools to:\n   - **List text sources** (e.g., narrative collections, interview sets)\n   - **List numeric datasets** (e.g., survey tables, EHR‑derived tables)\n2. For each candidate source:\n   - Fetch a **small sample** (e.g., a few narratives, a few rows of numeric data)\n   - Briefly describe:\n     - What the data represent\n     - How they relate to the research question\n3. Confirm with the user which sources to prioritize.\n\nUpdate the memo with:\n\n- Selected text sources and why\n- Selected numeric datasets and why\n\n### 4. Initial coding of qualitative data (open / exploratory)\n\n1. Select a **manageable subset** of text (e.g., 10–20 narratives or segments).\n2. Apply **open coding** using the CRISP‑T coding tools:\n   - Generate **short, grounded codes** that stay close to the data\n   - Avoid premature theory; focus on what participants are saying/doing/experiencing\n3. Use MCP tools to:\n   - Save codes to the project\n   - Attach codes to segments\n   - Retrieve and refine the emerging code list\n\nIn the memo:\n\n- Describe the coding approach (e.g., open coding, line‑by‑line, incident‑focused)\n- Provide **examples**: quote → code → brief interpretation\n\n### 5. Focused coding and category development\n\n1. Review the emerging code list using CRISP‑T tools (e.g., list codes, code frequencies).\n2. Group related codes into **higher‑level categories** or themes:\n   - Merge overlapping codes\n   - Distinguish closely related but conceptually different codes\n3. If the server supports it, create or update:\n   - A **codebook** (code name, definition, inclusion/exclusion criteria, example quotes)\n   - **Category structures** (e.g., parent/child relationships)\n\nIn the memo:\n\n- Describe key categories and how they were derived\n- Note any tensions, ambiguities, or alternative interpretations\n\n### 6. Computational triangulation with numeric data\n\nUsing CRISP‑T tools that link text and numeric data:\n\n1. **Identify the linkage key** (e.g., participant ID, case ID, encounter ID).\n2. For each case or group:\n   - Retrieve **coded qualitative data** (codes, categories, or themes)\n   - Retrieve **numeric variables** (e.g., age, scores, outcomes, counts)\n3. Construct **triangulation views**, such as:\n   - Code frequencies by group (e.g., theme prevalence by age band or outcome)\n   - Associations between codes and numeric indicators (e.g., high vs. low scores)\n   - Patterns of convergence (where qualitative and quantitative tell a similar story)\n   - Patterns of divergence (where they conflict or complicate each other)\n\nWhen tools support it, generate:\n\n- **Triangulation matrices** (e.g., codes × variables, cases × themes)\n- **Summary statistics** (e.g., counts, proportions, simple associations)\n\nIn the memo:\n\n- Describe **how** triangulation was done (data sources, linkage, variables)\n- Highlight **convergences, divergences, and surprises**\n- Emphasize that triangulation is about **enriching and challenging** interpretations, not “proving” them\n\n### 7. Synthesis and theory‑building\n\n1. Integrate insights from:\n   - Qualitative categories and themes\n   - Numeric patterns and contrasts\n   - Triangulation matrices and summaries\n2. Propose **tentative theoretical statements** or propositions:\n   - “In this context, participants who X tend to Y, especially when Z…”\n3. Explicitly note:\n   - Alternative explanations\n   - Data limitations\n   - What additional data or analysis would strengthen the claims\n\nUpdate the memo with:\n\n- A **coherent narrative** that links data, codes, categories, and numeric patterns\n- Clear statements about **what the data support** and **what remains uncertain**\n\n### 8. Export and documentation\n\n1. Use CRISP‑T export tools to save:\n   - Codebook(s)\n   - Triangulation matrices\n   - Any generated summaries or tables\n2. If supported, export:\n   - The analytic memo as Markdown or another requested format\n   - A machine‑readable representation of the analysis (e.g., JSON snapshot)\n\nProvide the user with:\n\n- A **human‑readable summary** (memo)\n- A **list of exported artifacts** and where they are stored (paths, IDs, or URLs)\n\n---\n\n## Model behavior and style guidelines\n\nWhen using this skill, you should:\n\n- **Be methodologically explicit**\n  - Name what you are doing (open coding, focused coding, triangulation, memoing)\n  - Briefly justify key analytic decisions\n- **Stay grounded in the data**\n  - Use short quotes and concrete examples\n  - Avoid over‑generalizing beyond what the data support\n- **Respect the user’s context**\n  - If they are teaching, highlight steps and rationale for students\n  - If they are writing a paper or grant, emphasize clarity and traceability\n- **Limit questions**\n  - Ask at most **one or two** focused questions at a time\n  - Default to reasonable assumptions when the user is not specific\n\n---\n\n## Limitations and cautions\n\n- Triangulation results should be treated as **aids to interpretation**, not definitive proof.\n- Always encourage the user to:\n  - Review codes and categories\n  - Challenge interpretations\n  - Consider ethical and contextual factors not visible in the data\n\n---\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-06T06:49:05.563Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for NLP Agents needing advanced qualitative research capabilities with vibe analytics and computational triangulation.","zh":"非常适合需要高级定性研究能力的NLP代理，包括气氛分析和计算三角测量。","ja":"NLPエージェントが高度な定性的研究能力を必要とする場合に最適です。バイブ分析や計算三角測定などの機能を備えています。","ko":"고급 질적 연구 능력 및 바이브 분석, 계산 삼각 측정을 필요로 하는 NLP 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de NLP que necesitan capacidades de investigación cualitativa avanzadas con análisis de vibraciones y triangulación computacional.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents NLP ayant besoin de capacités de recherche qualitative avancées avec analyse de vibrations et triangulation computationnelle.","de":"Perfekt für NLP-Agents, die erweiterte qualitative Forschungsfähigkeiten mit Schwingungsanalyse und computergestützter Triangulation benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de NLP que necessitam de capacidades de pesquisa qualitativa avançadas com análise de vibração e triangulação computacional.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов NLP, которым необходимы продвинутые качественные исследовательские возможности с вибрационной аналитикой и вычислительной триангуляцией.","ar":"مثالي لويبوتات NLP التي تحتاج إلى قدرات بحث نوعي متقدم مع تحليل الاهتزاز والثلاثية الحسابية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform AI-assisted qualitative research by linking textual narratives and numeric data using grounded theory-inspired coding and corpus management tools, leveraging the CRISP-T MCP server for comprehensive analysis.","zh":"通过使用接地理论启发的编码和语料库管理工具，链接文本叙述和数值数据，利用CRISP-T MCP服务器进行综合分析，从而使代理能够执行AI辅助的定性研究。","ja":"接地理論に基づくコーディングやコーパス管理ツールを使用して、テキストの物語と数値データをリンクし、CRISP-T MCPサーバーを使用して包括的な分析を実行することで、エージェントがAI支援の定性的研究を実行できるようにします。","ko":"데이터에 대한 심층 분석을 위해 기초이론에 기반한 코딩 및 말뭉치 관리 도구를 사용하여 텍스트 내러티브와 수치 데이터를 연결하고, CRISP-T MCP 서버를 활용하여 포괄적인 분석을 수행함으로써 에이전트가 AI 지원 질적 연구를 수행할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar investigaciones cualitativas asistidas por IA al vincular narrativas textuales y datos numéricos utilizando herramientas de codificación inspiradas en la teoría fundamentada y gestión de corpus, aprovechando el servidor CRISP-T MCP para un análisis integral.","fr":"Permet aux agents de réaliser des recherches qualitatives assistées par IA en reliant des récits textuels et des données numériques à l''aide d''outils de codage inspirés de la théorie ancrée et de gestion de corpus, en exploitant le serveur CRISP-T MCP pour une analyse complète.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, AI-gestützte qualitative Forschung durchzuführen, indem sie textuelle Erzählungen und numerische Daten mithilfe von grundlageninspirierten Codierungs- und Korpusmanagement-Tools verknüpfen, wobei der CRISP-T MCP-Server für eine umfassende Analyse genutzt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar pesquisas qualitativas assistidas por IA, vinculando narrativas textuais e dados numéricos usando codificação inspirada na teoria fundamentada e ferramentas de gerenciamento de corpus, aproveitando o servidor CRISP-T MCP para análise abrangente.","ru":"Позволяет агентам выполнять исследовательские работы по качественному анализу с помощью ИИ, связывая текстовые нарративы и числовые данные с помощью кодирования, вдохновленного основанной теорией, и инструментов управления корпусом, используя сервер CRISP-T MCP для всестороннего анализа.","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من إجراء بحث نوعي مدعوم بالذكاء الاصطناعي من خلال ربط السرد النصي والبيانات الرقمية باستخدام ترميز مستوحى من النظرية المضمنة وأدوات إدارة المجموعة، واستخدام خادم CRISP-T MCP للتحليل الشامل."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating qualitative analysis workflows with documented results","Generating insights from textual narratives and numeric data using computational triangulation","Applying grounded theory-inspired coding for in-depth data analysis"],"zh":["自动化具有文档化结果的定性分析工作流程","使用计算三角测量从文本叙述和数值数据中生成见解","应用接地理论启发的编码进行深入数据分析"],"ja":["文書化された結果を持つ定性的分析ワークフローを自動化する","計算三角測定を使用してテキストの物語と数値データからインサイトを生成する","接地理論に基づくコーディングを適用して深いデータ分析を実行する"],"ko":["문서화된 결과를 갖는 질적 분석 워크플로우를 자동화하는 것","계산 삼각 측정을 사용하여 텍스트 내러티브와 수치 데이터에서 통찰력을 생성하는 것","기초이론에 기반한 코딩을 적용하여 깊은 데이터 분석을 수행하는 것"],"es":["Automatizar flujos de trabajo de análisis cualitativo con resultados documentados","Generar información a partir de narrativas textuales y datos numéricos utilizando triangulación computacional","Aplicar codificación inspirada en la teoría fundamentada para un análisis de datos en profundidad"],"fr":["Automatiser les flux de travail d''analyse qualitative avec des résultats documentés","Générer des informations à partir de récits textuels et de données numériques en utilisant la triangulation computationnelle","Appliquer un codage inspiré de la théorie ancrée pour une analyse de données en profondeur"],"de":["Automatisierung qualitativer Analyse-Workflows mit dokumentierten Ergebnissen","Generierung von Erkenntnissen aus textuellen Erzählungen und numerischen Daten unter Verwendung computergestützter Triangulation","Anwendung grundlageninspirierter Codierung für eine tiefgehende Datenanalyse"],"pt":["Automatizar fluxos de trabalho de análise qualitativa com resultados documentados","Gerar insights a partir de narrativas textuais e dados numéricos usando triangulação computacional","Aplicar codificação inspirada na teoria fundamentada para análise de dados em profundidade"],"ru":["Автоматизировать рабочие потоки качественного анализа с задокументированными результатами","Генерировать идеи из текстовых нарративов и числовых данных с помощью вычислительной триангуляции","Применять кодирование, вдохновленное основанной теорией, для глубокого анализа данных"],"ar":["تأتمتية سير عمل التحليل النوعي مع نتائج مدوّنة","إنتاج رؤى من السرد النصي والبيانات الرقمية باستخدام الثلاثية الحسابية","تطبيق ترميز مستوحى من النظرية المضمنة لتحليل البيانات العميق"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to the CRISP-T MCP server","Limited to qualitative research and analysis tasks"],"zh":["需要访问CRISP-T MCP服务器","仅限于定性研究和分析任务"],"ja":["CRISP-T MCPサーバーへのアクセスが必要","定性的研究および分析タスクのみに限定される"],"ko":["CRISP-T MCP 서버에 대한 액세스가 필요","질적 연구 및 분석 태스크에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere acceso al servidor CRISP-T MCP","Limitado a tareas de investigación y análisis cualitativos"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au serveur CRISP-T MCP","Limité aux tâches de recherche et d''analyse qualitative"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf den CRISP-T MCP-Server","Begrenzt auf qualitative Forschungs- und Analyseaufgaben"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao servidor CRISP-T MCP","Limitado a tarefas de pesquisa e análise qualitativa"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к серверу CRISP-T MCP","Ограничен качественными исследовательскими и аналитическими задачами"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى خادم CRISP-T MCP","محدود بمهام البحث والتحليل النوعي"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"fcb7d601db4a386ea6e1520042c43c9d27111b990bdc518bbf37564c4e3c4ba2","qualityScore":50}');
